{"id": "EUVD-2026-67560", "enisaUuid": "4011698b-649c-3a58-a94d-80f409b77d47", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: pci: Fix NULL dereference on AIBV allocation failure\n\nThe airq_iv_create() can return NULL on failure, but the return value was\nnever checked. If it fails, zdev->aibv will be NULL and fail when\ndereferenced in kvm_zpci_set_airq(). Add a NULL check and free the\npreviously allocated AISB bit and zdev->aisb on failure.", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:52:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:26:33", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96099486b63985801c9c6ef22505e9aa635b2d20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a95abe964400771ad82b027d7b84a0d183cd0db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df947d85e164a50a29d43a96e814f69ab1d0f7ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e137d082325bbcae780087b57501d38585e625d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1a103dc9016c25e7423ce5841a5cc2df76d59f3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8bf09b9b7d3232806df95f409581f8a9fd99a3fa"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q4fh-xh4r-x3xp", "CVE-2026-80684"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1af6aabd-54b6-3009-9643-689d0dd2893b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.151"}, {"id": "1d3bc51d-cc0c-385b-9f50-8812f6dc86fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "2785fadd-bd9e-3f2c-bc6c-3f3991ccfe81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.103"}, {"id": "33f004c7-fd45-34ac-8080-75d06b707517", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3c5a1b6f0a18520a0edd0600fef6f1a8553b8fdc <d1a103dc9016c25e7423ce5841a5cc2df76d59f3"}, {"id": "46be5f42-69a7-3b19-bf1a-7c32c97978ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": 